{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Antifungal, candidacidal, anti-sepsis, Hemolytic", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals this sequence is most similar (38.46%) to P-02 K: 16%; GRAVY: -0.524; M. Wt: 3088.594; Mol formula: C149H220N37O35; Mol Ex Coeff: 8530; Activity: zone inhibition: active against E. coli (MIC 2.5 uM), P. aeruginosa, S. aureus (MIC 5-20 uM), and C. albicans ( Kasetty et al., 2011). In vitro toxicity: ~60% hemolysis at 60 uM: HC50 ~50 uM. Animal model:mouse: protect against P. aeruginosa sepsis, mainly via reduction of both systemic cytokine responses and excessive coagulation. Anti-inflammatory: GKY25 binds to LPS and interferes with TLR4/myeloid differentiation protein-2 dimerization, leading to inhibition of TLR4 dimerization and subsequent reduction of NF-kB activity and pro-inflammatory cytokine production in monocytes and macrophages ( Hansen et al., 2015). The original entry kalata B9 linear has been merged with entry 1108 due to the same sequence.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "20421939", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "PLoS Pathog. 2010 Apr 22;6(4):e1000857. doi: 10.1371/journal.ppat.1000857. Pub-Med.", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP01132", "source_id": "AP01132", "source_numeric_id": "01132", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP01132", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Proteolysis of human thrombin generates novel host defense peptides.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
